{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-03T21:43:04.919Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"436e44ca2d204a1ee603915a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1655","claim:pm-mrvq8u","claim:pm-thbdxu","lineage:pm-thbdxu","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1655+pm-mrvq8u+pm-thbdxu","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1655","claim:pm-mrvq8u","claim:pm-thbdxu","lineage:pm-thbdxu","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.317","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-03T21:43:04.919Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-03T21:43:04.919Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implemented all four. (1) docs/CONFIGURATION.md governance.start_blocker_enforcement row names update --status in_progress, claim --start, claim --next --start and start-task, and says claim --next --start skips a refused candidate; docs/COMMANDS.md documents start_refused. (2) ItemRevisionConflictRowFields is exported from the SDK root; sdk/public-surface.json records it as an additive symbol. (3) claimNextFromRecommendations (src/sdk/lifecycle/claim.ts) skips a candidate refused with start_blocked_by_open_dependency (the refusal fires inside the claim's locked mutation, so nothing is written to it), claims the next candidate, and reports skipped ids as start_refused on the available and if-available results and in details.start_refused of the exhausted refusal, whose why now distinguishes start refusals from claims by other agents. Spec: tests/unit/sdk/lifecycle/start-race.spec.ts drives a real tracker where the blocker edge lands after ranking; the refused candidate's history is unchanged. (4) postCloseDependentConflict (src/sdk/lifecycle/close.ts) replaces the dependent conflict's required/nextSteps: the close is complete and must not be retried, and the only remaining step is re-reading and unblocking the dependent with pm update <dep> --status open --unset blocked_by --unset blocked_reason --expect-hash <dep>=<item_hash>. That command was verified in a sandbox (status open, blocked_by edge removed). Spec assertions in tests/unit/sdk/lifecycle/item-revision.spec.ts."}]}],"before_hash":"33bba08ec789a30a4ae8936822558967ef5eb94918d0072abf4c74fb1109313d","after_hash":"bc756800ec283484c8e08343097a8e87e4e338c17b797fe0449c50075436bf37","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"26399dd76efcedbaa131235326eeaeb85d1280655d0173f389e145f4f0d65359"}
